<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- Inspire RH56E2 left hand: xacro macro `inspire_hand_e2_left`.

     Source: inspire_rh56e2_hand_description/urdf/inspire_hand_e2_left_macro.xacro
             (renesas-rdk/inspire_rh56e2_hand, Apache-2.0), generated by the vendor from
             Inspire's SolidWorks export RH56E2_L_2025_9_10.urdf.
     Changes from the vendor file, nothing else:
       - mesh paths -> package://g1_edu_inspire_rh56e2_description/meshes/hand_left/
       - base_link.STL renamed left_base_link.STL (MuJoCo names meshes after their
         file, and both hands had a base_link.STL)
       - colours as on the real hand, with named materials instead of name="":
         flange (hand_base_link) silver, back cover (palm_2) white, everything else black
       - inertials of palm_1 and the 12 digit links, written by
         tools/compute_hand_inertials.py (do not edit them by hand): the hand weighs
         868.1 g, the 888.5 g of the real hand with its wrist coupler on the scale minus
         the coupler's 20.4 g (the coupler is a link of the robot xacro). Digits keep the
         vendor's masses, palm_1 takes the rest (475.26 g); centres of mass and tensors
         are those of each link's mesh, as the vendor's put every left-hand digit's CoM
         outside the digit. See "Inspire RH56E2 inertials" in the README.
     Same STL for visual and collision, joints, limits and <mimic> tags as the vendor's;
     inertials of hand_base_link, palm_2 and the force-sensor links also the vendor's.

     Usage:
       <xacro:inspire_hand_e2_left prefix="left_" parent="some_link">
         <origin xyz="..." rpy="..."/>   pose of left_base (centre of the top face of the
       </xacro:inspire_hand_e2_left>    flange, z along the hand) in some_link

     Frames: ${prefix}base: z out of the flange towards the fingertips, x out of the palm.
             ${prefix}hand_base_link: base rotated by pi about x (vendor CAD frame).
     Actuated joints (6): ${prefix}thumb_proximal_yaw_joint, ${prefix}thumb_proximal_pitch_joint,
       ${prefix}index_proximal_joint, ${prefix}middle_proximal_joint,
       ${prefix}ring_proximal_joint, ${prefix}pinky_proximal_joint
     Mimic joints (6):
       ${prefix}thumb_intermediate_joint = 0.8392    x thumb_proximal_pitch_joint
       ${prefix}thumb_distal_joint       = 0.7477272 x thumb_proximal_pitch_joint
       ${prefix}<finger>_intermediate_joint = 1.0843 x <finger>_proximal_joint -->
